<https://registry.inspire.gv.at/codelist/oerok-flaecheninanspruchnahme/103> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The category '103 – Municipal and other roads' is arguably the most heterogeneous road category. It encompasses all municipal roads as well as internal settlement access roads, access and exit ramps, cycle paths, and agricultural access roads (Güterwege).\nBy definition, forestry roads and alpine pasture roads are not included. Since there is no uniform classification of forestry roads in the GIP (Graph Integration Platform), forestry roads were identified using federal-state-specific queries as well as the forest layer of the BFW (Federal Research and Training Centre for Forests). \nIn the agricultural sector, agricultural access roads are also systematically adjusted based on INVEKOS (IACS) agricultural parcel boundaries. This ensures that no road overlaps an utilized agricultural area."@en <https://registry.inspire.gv.at/codelist/oerok-flaecheninanspruchnahme:1> .
<https://registry.inspire.gv.at/codelist/oerok-flaecheninanspruchnahme/641> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> <https://registry.inspire.gv.at/codelist/oerok-flaecheninanspruchnahme:1> .
