<https://registry.inspire.gv.at/codelist/oerok-flaecheninanspruchnahme/520> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "In addition to the specific location of the wind turbine, the wind turbines also contain the service entrances, unless these are already recorded in the traffic module anyway. Since the wind turbines are registered in the aviation obstacle database, the size, distribution and timeliness of these turbines are very well known and accurately reproduced. Since wind turbines are usually built over formerly landscaped areas, a very accurate"@en <https://registry.inspire.gv.at/codelist/oerok-flaecheninanspruchnahme:1> .
<https://registry.inspire.gv.at/codelist/oerok-flaecheninanspruchnahme/413> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "no evaluation category, only survey category: supply and disposal areas according to the DLM of the Bev (category 2801 power poles)"@en <https://registry.inspire.gv.at/codelist/oerok-flaecheninanspruchnahme:1> .
<https://registry.inspire.gv.at/codelist/oerok-flaecheninanspruchnahme/101> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The evaluation category 'Motorways and expressways' encompasses all roads and ancillary land managed by ASFINAG that are not used for agriculture or forestry. Wooded patches within motorway junctions are excluded if they are recorded in the forest layer. Access and exit ramps as well as service areas and toll plazas are considered part of the motorway."@en <https://registry.inspire.gv.at/codelist/oerok-flaecheninanspruchnahme:1> .
